@startuml 13-state-diagram
title Order lifecycle - state diagram (bonus)
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> CREATED : checkout succeeded\n(payment taken, stock reserved)

CREATED --> CONFIRMED : confirm()
CREATED --> CANCELLED : cancel()\n[fee 0, refund 100%]
CREATED --> CREATED : editItems()

CONFIRMED --> PREPARING : startPreparing()
CONFIRMED --> CANCELLED : cancel()\n[fee 10%, refund 90%]

PREPARING --> DELIVERING : startDelivery()\n[type requires courier]
PREPARING --> DELIVERED : markDelivered()\n[pickup]

DELIVERING --> DELIVERED : markDelivered()

DELIVERED --> DELIVERED : requestRefund()\n[paid online, within 24h, once]
DELIVERED --> DELIVERED : rate(1..5)\n[once]

CANCELLED --> [*]

state CREATED : edit items: yes\ncancel: free
state CONFIRMED : edit items: no\ncancel: 10% fee
state PREPARING : edit: no, cancel: no
state DELIVERING : edit: no, cancel: no\ncourier location visible
state DELIVERED : rate (once), refund window 24h\n(not for cash on delivery)
state CANCELLED : terminal

note bottom
  Any operation not drawn for a state is rejected with
  IllegalOrderOperationException (no state change, no event).
  Delivery and scheduled orders pass through DELIVERING; pickup orders skip it.
end note
@enduml
